.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH thurvsa 1  "thurvsa 0.1.0-dev.4" 
.SH NAME
thurvsa \- ThurVSA Management CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBthurvsa\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-copyright\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
ThurVSA Management CLI
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to configuration file.

Defaults to `/etc/thurvtl/thurvtl.yaml` (thurvtl) or `/etc/thurvsa/thurvsa.yaml` (thurvsa).
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
User to drop privileges to under sudo.

Only applied by daemon\-down commands that write under `data_dir`. Under plain `sudo` those files would otherwise be owned by root and unreadable by the daemon. No effect when the CLI is already running as a non\-root user. Defaults to `thurvtl` (thurvtl) or `thurvsa` (thurvsa).
.TP
\fB\-\-copyright\fR
Print the copyright + license notice and exit.

Handled by [`handle_copyright_flag`] before `Cli::parse()`, so the flag works without a subcommand. Declared here too so it shows up in `\-\-help`.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
thurvsa\-volume(1)
Volume management (create, list, info, destroy)
.TP
thurvsa\-system(1)
System operations
.TP
thurvsa\-iscsi(1)
iSCSI CHAP credentials
.TP
thurvsa\-nvmetcp(1)
NVMe\-TCP TLS\-PSK credentials
.TP
thurvsa\-config(1)
Configuration helpers (defaults yaml, systemd unit, shell completion)
.TP
thurvsa\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0\-dev.4
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/thurvsa/thurvsa.yaml
Daemon configuration. Minimal starter shipped at install; the
full annotated reference for every key is at
.IR /usr/share/doc/thurvsa/thurvsa.defaults.yaml .
.TP
.I /run/thurvsa/admin.sock
Admin Unix socket the CLI dials for daemon-routed verbs (mode
0660, peer-cred authed).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thurvsad (8)
